============================================================================================
  Launch-copy headline numbers
============================================================================================

  Today (Stage 1, off-the-shelf tokenizer):
    vs pure-Python:   8.5x fewer LLM tokens (88% savings)
    vs sympy-Python:  2.0x fewer LLM tokens (+50% savings)

  Stage 2 (fine-tuned vocabulary, 1 op = 1 LLM token):
    vs sympy-Python:  3.2x fewer LLM tokens (68% savings)

  Stage 3 (integer-sequence LOVA, bytes == LLM tokens):
    vs sympy-Python:  2.4x fewer LLM tokens (59% savings)

  Caveats:
    - Python imports counted once per solution (per-file overhead).
    - Stage 2 assumes a fine-tuned tokenizer; no model trained yet.
    - Stage 3 assumes canonical integer form (no text surface).
    - LOVABench v2 is number-theory-heavy; other domains would vary.
    - Per-category breakdown above shows LOVA's edge is 2-3x larger
      on deep-compose / conserve than on surprise / let-heavy.

